    <stringTable>
      <string id="3rdparty_Extensions">3rdparty › Extensions</string>
      <string id="3rdparty_Extensions_Explain">Provide configuration to WebExtensions, which they can read through the storage.managed API.

Allow WebExtensions to configure policy. For more information, see Adding policy support to your extension (https://extensionworkshop.com/documentation/enterprise/enterprise-development/#how-to-add-policy).

For GPO and Intune, the extension developer should provide an ADMX file.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#3rdparty-policies-for-extensions
</string>
      <string id="AIControls_Default">AIControls › Default</string>
      <string id="AIControls_Default_Explain">Controls the default state for AI features listed below, unless they are explicitly configured in the policy.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#aicontrols

Locked: If true, the user cannot change the setting.
</string>
      <string id="AIControls_Default_Value_available">Available</string>
      <string id="AIControls_Default_Value_blocked">Blocked</string>
      <string id="AIControls_Translations">AIControls › Translations</string>
