      <string id="ContentAnalysis_InterceptionPoints_Clipboard">ContentAnalysis › InterceptionPoints › Clipboard</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_InterceptionPoints_Clipboard_Explain">Controls clipboard operations for files and text.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#contentanalysis

Enabled: Indicates whether clipboard operations should use DLP. The default is true.

PlainTextOnly: Indicates whether to only analyze the text/plain format on the clipboard. If this value is false, all formats will be analyzed, which some DLP agents may not expect. Regardless of this value, files will be analyzed as usual. The default is true.
</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_InterceptionPoints_ClipboardCopy">ContentAnalysis › InterceptionPoints › ClipboardCopy</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_InterceptionPoints_ClipboardCopy_Explain">Controls settings for specific interception points.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#contentanalysis
</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_InterceptionPoints_Download">ContentAnalysis › InterceptionPoints › Download</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_InterceptionPoints_Download_Explain">Controls download operations. (Firefox 142, Firefox ESR 140.2)

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#contentanalysis

Enabled: Indicates whether download operations should use DLP. The default is false.
</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_InterceptionPoints_DragAndDrop">ContentAnalysis › InterceptionPoints › DragAndDrop</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_InterceptionPoints_DragAndDrop_Explain">Controls drag and drop operations for files and text.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#contentanalysis

Enabled: Indicates whether drag and drop operations should use DLP. The default is true.

PlainTextOnly: Indicates whether to only analyze the text/plain format in what is being dropped. If this value is false, all formats will be analyzed, which some DLP agents may not expect. Regardless of this value, files will be analyzed as usual. The default is true.
</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_InterceptionPoints_FileUpload">ContentAnalysis › InterceptionPoints › FileUpload</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_InterceptionPoints_FileUpload_Explain">Controls file upload operations for files chosen from the file picker.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#contentanalysis

Enabled: Indicates whether file upload operations should use DLP. The default is true.
</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_InterceptionPoints_Print">ContentAnalysis › InterceptionPoints › Print</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_InterceptionPoints_Print_Explain">Controls print operations.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#contentanalysis

Enabled: Indicates whether print operations should use DLP. The default is true.
</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_Enabled">ContentAnalysis › Enabled</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_Enabled_Explain">Indicates whether Firefox should use DLP. Note that if this value is true and no DLP agent is running, all DLP requests will be denied unless DefaultResult is set to 1 or 2.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#contentanalysis
</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_PipePathName">Pipe Path Name</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_PipePathName_Explain">The name of the pipe the DLP agent has created and Firefox will connect to. The default is "path_user".

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#contentanalysis
</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_AgentTimeout">Agent Timeout</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_AgentTimeout_Explain">The timeout in number of seconds after a DLP request is sent to the agent. After this timeout, the request will be denied unless TimeoutResult is set to 1 or 2. The default is 300.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#contentanalysis
</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_AllowUrlRegexList">Allow Url Regex List</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_AllowUrlRegexList_Explain">A space-separated list of regular expressions that indicates URLs for which DLP operations will always be allowed without consulting the agent. The default is "^about:(?!blank|srcdoc).*", meaning that any pages that start with "about:" will be exempt from DLP except for "about:blank" and "about:srcdoc", as these can be controlled by web content.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#contentanalysis
</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_DenyUrlRegexList">Deny Url Regex List</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_DenyUrlRegexList_Explain">A space-separated list of regular expressions that indicates URLs for which DLP operations will always be denied without consulting the agent. The default is the empty string.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#contentanalysis
</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_AgentName">Agent Name</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_AgentName_Explain">The name of the DLP agent. This is used in dialogs and notifications about DLP operations. The default is "A DLP Agent".

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#contentanalysis
</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_ClientSignature">Client Signature</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_ClientSignature_Explain">Indicates the required signature of the DLP agent connected to the pipe. If this is a non-empty string and the DLP agent does not have a signature with a Subject Name that exactly matches this value, Firefox will not connect to the pipe. The default is the empty string.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#contentanalysis
</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_IsPerUser">Is Per User</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_IsPerUser_Explain">Indicates whether the pipe the DLP agent has created is per-user or per-system. The default is true, meaning per-user.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#contentanalysis
</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_MaxConnectionsCount">ContentAnalysis › MaxConnectionsCount</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_MaxConnectionsCount_Explain">Configure Firefox to use an agent for Data Loss Prevention (DLP) that is compatible with the Google Chrome Content Analysis Connector Agent SDK.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#contentanalysis
</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_ShowBlockedResult">Show Blocked Result</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_ShowBlockedResult_Explain">Indicates whether Firefox should show a notification when a DLP request is denied. The default is true.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#contentanalysis
</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_DefaultResult">Default Result</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_DefaultResult_Explain">Indicates the desired behavior for DLP requests if there is a problem connecting to the DLP agent. The default is 0.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#contentanalysis
</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_TimeoutResult">Timeout Result</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_TimeoutResult_Explain">Indicates the desired behavior for DLP requests if the DLP agent does not respond to a request in less than AgentTimeout seconds. The default is 0.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#contentanalysis
</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_BypassForSameTabOperations">Bypass For Same Tab Operations</string>
      <string id="ContentAnalysis_BypassForSameTabOperations_Explain">Indicates whether Firefox will automatically allow DLP requests whose data comes from the same tab and frame - for example, if data is copied to the clipboard and then pasted on the same page. The default is false.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#contentanalysis
</string>
      <string id="Cookies_Allow">Allowed Sites</string>
      <string id="Cookies_Allow_Explain">Cookies are always allowed for these origins (not domains). Each must include http or https.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#cookies
</string>
      <string id="Cookies_AllowSession">Allowed Sites (Session Only)</string>
      <string id="Cookies_AllowSession_Explain">Cookies are only allowed for the current session for these origins (not domains). Each must include http or https.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#cookies
</string>
      <string id="Cookies_Block">Blocked Sites</string>
      <string id="Cookies_Block_Explain">Cookies are always blocked for these origins (not domains). Each must include http or https.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#cookies
</string>
      <string id="Cookies_Default">Accept cookies from websites (deprecated)</string>
      <string id="Cookies_Default_Explain">Deprecated.

Determines whether cookies are accepted at all. Use Behavior instead.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#cookies
</string>
      <string id="Cookies_AcceptThirdParty">Accept third-party cookies (deprecated)</string>
      <string id="Cookies_AcceptThirdParty_Explain">Deprecated.

Determines how third-party cookies are handled. Use Behavior instead.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#cookies
</string>
      <string id="Cookies_AcceptThirdParty_always">Always</string>
      <string id="Cookies_AcceptThirdParty_never">Never</string>
      <string id="Cookies_AcceptThirdParty_from_visited">From visited sites only</string>
      <string id="Cookies_RejectTracker">Reject trackers (deprecated)</string>
      <string id="Cookies_RejectTracker_Explain">Deprecated.

Only rejects cookies for trackers. Use Behavior instead.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#cookies
</string>
      <string id="Cookies_ExpireAtSessionEnd">Keep cookies until Firefox is closed (deprecated)</string>
      <string id="Cookies_ExpireAtSessionEnd_Explain">Deprecated.

Determines when cookies expire. Use SanitizeOnShutdown (#sanitizeonshutdown) instead.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#cookies
</string>
      <string id="Cookies_Locked">Do not allow preferences to be changed</string>
      <string id="Cookies_Locked_Explain">Prevents the user from changing cookie preferences.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#cookies
</string>
      <string id="Cookies_Behavior">Cookie Behavior</string>
      <string id="Cookies_Behavior_Explain">Sets the default behavior for cookies.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#cookies
</string>
      <string id="Cookies_Behavior_accept">Accept all cookies</string>
      <string id="Cookies_Behavior_reject_foreign">Reject third-party cookies</string>
      <string id="Cookies_Behavior_reject">Reject all cookies</string>
      <string id="Cookies_Behavior_limit_foreign">Third-party cookies from visited sites only</string>
      <string id="Cookies_Behavior_reject_tracker">Reject known trackers</string>
      <string id="Cookies_Behavior_reject_tracker_and_partition_foreign">Reject known trackers and partition third-party cookies</string>
      <string id="Cookies_Behavior_partition_foreign">Partition third-party cookies</string>
      <string id="Cookies_BehaviorPrivateBrowsing">Cookie Behavior in private browsing</string>
      <string id="Cookies_BehaviorPrivateBrowsing_Explain">Sets the default behavior for cookies in private browsing.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#cookies
</string>
      <string id="Cookies_BehaviorPrivateBrowsing_accept">Accept all cookies</string>
      <string id="Cookies_BehaviorPrivateBrowsing_reject_foreign">Reject third-party cookies</string>
      <string id="Cookies_BehaviorPrivateBrowsing_reject">Reject all cookies</string>
      <string id="Cookies_BehaviorPrivateBrowsing_limit_foreign">Third-party cookies from visited sites only</string>
      <string id="Cookies_BehaviorPrivateBrowsing_reject_tracker">Reject known trackers</string>
      <string id="Cookies_BehaviorPrivateBrowsing_reject_tracker_and_partition_foreign">Reject known trackers and partition third-party cookies</string>
      <string id="Cookies_BehaviorPrivateBrowsing_partition_foreign">Partition third-party cookies</string>
      <string id="DefaultBrowserSettingEnabled">Enable default browser setting</string>
      <string id="DefaultBrowserSettingEnabled_Explain">Control whether the user can set Firefox as the default browser. If set to false, the default browser check is disabled and the controls for setting Firefox as the default browser are removed from the preferences.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#defaultbrowsersettingenabled
</string>
      <string id="DefaultDownloadDirectory">Default Download Directory</string>
      <string id="DefaultDownloadDirectory_Explain">Set the default download directory.

You can use ${home} for the native home directory.

Environment variables like %USERPROFILE% are expanded.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#defaultdownloaddirectory
</string>
      <string id="DefaultSerialGuardSetting">Control use of the Web Serial API</string>
      <string id="DefaultSerialGuardSetting_Explain">Set the default permission for websites requesting access to serial ports through the Web Serial API.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#defaultserialguardsetting
</string>
      <string id="DefaultSerialGuardSetting_2">Block serial port access</string>
      <string id="DefaultSerialGuardSetting_3">Ask when a site requests access</string>
      <string id="DisableAccounts">Disable Accounts</string>
      <string id="DisableAccounts_Explain">Disable account-based services, including sync.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#disableaccounts
</string>
      <string id="DisableAppUpdate">Disable Update</string>
      <string id="DisableAppUpdate_Explain">Turn off application updates within Firefox.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#disableappupdate
</string>
      <string id="DisableBuiltinPDFViewer">Disable Built-in PDF Viewer (PDF.js)</string>
      <string id="DisableBuiltinPDFViewer_Explain">Disable the built in PDF viewer.

PDF files are downloaded and sent externally.

Note: As of Firefox 140, this policy no longer completely disables PDF.js; it changes the handler to send PDF files to the operating system. Embedded PDF files are shown in the browser. If you need to completely disable PDF.js, you can use the PDFjs (#pdfjs) policy.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#disablebuiltinpdfviewer
</string>
      <string id="DisabledCiphers_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256">DisabledCiphers › TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256</string>
      <string id="DisabledCiphers_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256_Explain">Disable specific cryptographic ciphers, listed below.

Preferences Affected: security.ssl3.ecdhe_rsa_aes_128_gcm_sha256, security.ssl3.ecdhe_ecdsa_aes_128_gcm_sha256, security.ssl3.ecdhe_ecdsa_chacha20_poly1305_sha256, security.ssl3.ecdhe_rsa_chacha20_poly1305_sha256, security.ssl3.ecdhe_ecdsa_aes_256_gcm_sha384, security.ssl3.ecdhe_rsa_aes_256_gcm_sha384, security.ssl3.ecdhe_rsa_aes_128_sha, security.ssl3.ecdhe_ecdsa_aes_128_sha, security.ssl3.ecdhe_rsa_aes_256_sha, security.ssl3.ecdhe_ecdsa_aes_256_sha, security.ssl3.dhe_rsa_aes_128_sha, security.ssl3.dhe_rsa_aes_256_sha, security.ssl3.rsa_aes_128_gcm_sha256, security.ssl3.rsa_aes_256_gcm_sha384, security.ssl3.rsa_aes_128_sha, security.ssl3.rsa_aes_256_sha, security.ssl3.deprecated.rsa_des_ede3_sha, security.tls13.chacha20_poly1305_sha256, security.tls13.aes_128_gcm_sha256, security.tls13.aes_256_gcm_sha384

Note:

This policy was updated in Firefox 78 to allow enabling ciphers as well. Setting the value to true disables the cipher, setting the value to false enables the cipher. Previously setting the value to true or false disabled the cipher.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#disabledciphers
</string>
