      <string id="FirefoxHome_Locked_Explain">Customize the Firefox Home page.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#firefoxhome
</string>
      <string id="FirefoxSuggest_WebSuggestions">Suggestions from the web</string>
      <string id="FirefoxSuggest_WebSuggestions_Explain">Customize Firefox Suggest (US only).

As of Firefox 146, WebSuggestions turns off Suggest completely.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#firefoxsuggest
</string>
      <string id="FirefoxSuggest_SponsoredSuggestions">Suggestions from sponsors</string>
      <string id="FirefoxSuggest_SponsoredSuggestions_Explain">Customize Firefox Suggest (US only).

As of Firefox 146, WebSuggestions turns off Suggest completely.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#firefoxsuggest
</string>
      <string id="FirefoxSuggest_ImproveSuggest">Improve the Firefox Suggest experience</string>
      <string id="FirefoxSuggest_ImproveSuggest_Explain">Customize Firefox Suggest (US only).

As of Firefox 146, WebSuggestions turns off Suggest completely.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#firefoxsuggest
</string>
      <string id="FirefoxSuggest_OnlineEnabled">FirefoxSuggest › OnlineEnabled</string>
      <string id="FirefoxSuggest_OnlineEnabled_Explain">Customize Firefox Suggest (US only).

As of Firefox 146, WebSuggestions turns off Suggest completely.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#firefoxsuggest
</string>
      <string id="FirefoxSuggest_Locked">Do not allow preferences to be changed</string>
      <string id="FirefoxSuggest_Locked_Explain">Customize Firefox Suggest (US only).

As of Firefox 146, WebSuggestions turns off Suggest completely.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#firefoxsuggest
</string>
      <string id="GenerativeAI_Chatbot">GenerativeAI › Chatbot</string>
      <string id="GenerativeAI_Chatbot_Explain">Controls access to AI chatbots in the sidebar. If false, AI chatbots are not available in the sidebar.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#generativeai
</string>
      <string id="GenerativeAI_SmartWindow">GenerativeAI › SmartWindow</string>
      <string id="GenerativeAI_SmartWindow_Explain">Configure generative AI features.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#generativeai
</string>
      <string id="GenerativeAI_LinkPreviews">Link Previews</string>
      <string id="GenerativeAI_LinkPreviews_Explain">(Firefox 144+) Controls whether AI is used to generate link previews. If false, AI is not used to generate link previews.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#generativeai
</string>
      <string id="GenerativeAI_TabGroups">Tab Groups</string>
      <string id="GenerativeAI_TabGroups_Explain">(Firefox 144+) Controls whether AI is used to suggest names and tabs for tab groups. If false, AI is not used to suggest names or tabs for tab groups.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#generativeai
</string>
      <string id="GenerativeAI_Enabled">GenerativeAI › Enabled</string>
      <string id="GenerativeAI_Enabled_Explain">Controls whether generative AI features are enabled by default. If false, all generative AI features are disabled by default. Individual generative AI policies can override this setting.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#generativeai
</string>
      <string id="GenerativeAI_Locked">Do not allow preferences to be changed</string>
      <string id="GenerativeAI_Locked_Explain">Prevents the user from changing generative AI preferences.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#generativeai
</string>
      <string id="GoToIntranetSiteForSingleWordEntryInAddressBar">Force direct intranet site navigation on single word entries in the address bar</string>
      <string id="GoToIntranetSiteForSingleWordEntryInAddressBar_Explain">Whether to always go through the DNS server before sending a single word search string to a search engine.

If the site exists, it will navigate to the website. If the intranet responds with a 404, the page will show a 404. If the intranet does not respond, the browser will attempt a search.

The second result in the URL bar will be a search result to allow users to conduct a web search exactly as it was entered.

If instead you would like to enable the ability to have your domain appear as a valid URL and to disallow the browser from ever searching that term using the first result that matches it, add the pref browser.fixup.domainwhitelist.YOUR_DOMAIN (where YOUR_DOMAIN is the name of the domain you'd like to add), and set the pref to true. The URL bar will then suggest YOUR_DOMAIN when the user fully types YOUR_DOMAIN. If the user attempts to load that domain and it fails to load, it will show an "Unable to connect" error page.

You can also whitelist a domain suffix that is not part of the Public Suffix List (https://publicsuffix.org/) by adding the pref browser.fixup.domainsuffixwhitelist.YOUR_DOMAIN_SUFFIX with a value of true.

Additionally, if you want users to see a "Did you mean to go to 'YOUR_DOMAIN'" prompt below the URL bar if they land on a search results page instead of an intranet domain that provides a response, set the pref browser.urlbar.dnsResolveSingleWordsAfterSearch to 1. Enabling this will cause the browser to commit a DNS check after every single word search. If the browser receives a response from the intranet, a prompt will ask the user if they'd like to instead navigate to YOUR_DOMAIN. If the user presses the yes button, browser.fixup.domainwhitelist.YOUR_DOMAIN will be set to true.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#gotointranetsiteforsinglewordentryinaddressbar
</string>
      <string id="Handlers">Handlers</string>
      <string id="Handlers_Explain">Configure default application handlers.

This policy is based on the internal format of handlers.json.

You can configure handlers based on a mime type (mimeTypes), a file's extension (extensions), or a protocol (schemes).

Within each handler type, you specify the given mimeType/extension/scheme as a key and use the following subkeys to describe how it is handled.

(mimeTypes|extensions|schemes)
  [name]
    action
      saveToDisk: Download the file instead of opening it.
      useHelperApp: Open the content with an application listed in handlers.
      useSystemDefault: Open the content with the application the operating system associates with that type.
    ask
    handlers
      name
      path
      uriTemplate

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#handlers
</string>
      <string id="HandlersOneLine">Handlers (one JSON line)</string>
      <string id="HandlersOneLine_Explain">Configure default application handlers.

This policy is based on the internal format of handlers.json.

You can configure handlers based on a mime type (mimeTypes), a file's extension (extensions), or a protocol (schemes).

Within each handler type, you specify the given mimeType/extension/scheme as a key and use the following subkeys to describe how it is handled.

(mimeTypes|extensions|schemes)
  [name]
    action
      saveToDisk: Download the file instead of opening it.
      useHelperApp: Open the content with an application listed in handlers.
      useSystemDefault: Open the content with the application the operating system associates with that type.
    ask
    handlers
      name
      path
      uriTemplate

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/firefox/policies/main/#handlers
</string>
